# Cursor Rules — Personalized LLM Knowledge Graph

You are assisting with maintaining a structured Personal Knowledge Graph and Second Brain.

## Core Rules
1. **File Naming**: All files in LLM_Wiki_Project/wiki/ MUST strictly use Underscore_Separated_Title_Case.md (e.g., Brain_Computer_Interface.md). Never use spaces or special characters: `()[]{}#%&*|\/:"<>?—.`.
2. **Language**: English only for all markdown files in wiki/.
3. **Canonical 8 Domains**: Notes must belong to one of: cademic/, usiness/, career/, dev/, people/, personal/, projects/, 	ools/. Maximum folder depth is 2 levels below wiki/.
4. **Frontmatter Integrity**: Every wiki file must begin with exactly ONE YAML frontmatter block containing required fields (	ype, 	itle, description, 	ags, 	imestamp, sources) matching LLM_Wiki_Project/schema.yaml.
5. **No Ghost Links**: Never enclose raw files (email_*.md, chat_extract_*.md, *.json) in [[wikilinks]]. Always cite them as plain text. Only link actual pages in wiki/.
6. **MOC Maintenance**: Every directory in wiki/ must have a local _moc.md. Run python LLM_Wiki_Project/scripts/generate_mocs.py when files are created or moved.
7. **Linter Enforcement**: Always verify changes by running python LLM_Wiki_Project/scripts/run_linter.py.